  "question": {
    "text": "An electric dipole is placed at a distance of 2 cm from an infinite plane sheet having positive charge density $\\sigma_{\\mathrm{o}}$. Choose the correct option from the following.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/Gn2asKgm1ffQ88sGYKMh4a6vTEncBGUgF4eqytt8P_0.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rcyfi",
      "text": "Potential energy and torque both are maximum.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vYDNE",
      "text": "Torque on dipole is zero and net force is directed away from the sheet.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sYs9f",
      "text": "Torque on dipole is zero and net force acts towards the sheet.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1vchh",
      "text": "Potential energy of dipole is minimum and torque is zero.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Electric field due to sheet $E=\\frac{\\sigma}{2 \\varepsilon_0}$ \r\nand torque on dipole $\\vec{\\tau}=\\vec{P} \\times \\vec{E}$ \r\nhere $\\vec{\\tau}=0$ \r\nand $U=-\\vec{P} \\cdot \\vec{E} \\rightarrow$ should be minimum",
    "image": null
  },
